SYNTHESIS
================================================================================
Doubling vertices turns a tournament edge into a fiberwise double round robin.
The old winner is not stored as a quotient score; every doubled pair ties 2-2.
It is stored in which perfect matching of the 2x2 block carries the old edge.
The hidden matching choices form a signed 2-lift; modulo sheet flips there are
2^C(n-1,2) choices, the same cube dimension as fixed-base tournament tilings.
